    "How would you explain, step by step, how to find the stationary points of an equation y=f(x)?": "To find stationary points, take the first derivative f’(x) and set it equal to zero. Solve for x to get critical points. Then, substitute these x-values back into f(x) to find the corresponding y-values. You can also check if they’re maxima or minima using the second derivative test.",
